##* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Gerard Brandt|chapter=Book XXXIII|translator=[anonymous]|title=The History of the Reformation and Other Ecclesiastical Transactions in and about the Low-countries, from the Beginning of the Eighth Century, down to the Famous Synod of Dort, inclusive.{{nb...|In which All the Revolutions that Happen’d in Church and State, on Account of the Divisions between the Protestants and Papists, the Arminians and Calvininsts, are Fairly and Fully Represented by the Reverend and Learned Mr. Gerard Brandt, Late Professor of Divinity, and Minister to the Protestant Remonstrants at Amsterdam. Faithfully Translated from the Original Low-Dutch.}}|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed by}} T[homas] Wood, for John Nicks,{{nb...|at the White-Hart at the West End of St. Paul’s Church-Yard.}}|year=1722|volume=III|page=24|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=KhxaAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA24|oclc=1227582867|passage=In the mean while, it was reſolved at the Synod, that ſince they muſt wait for the cited ''Remonſtrants'', they would enter upon ſome of the '''''Gravamina''''', or Points of Grievance which the Churches had laid before the Provincial Synods.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|author=James Wayland Joyce|chapter=English Synods. From the Accession of Archbishop [[w:John Peckham|John de Peccham]] to the Death of Archbishop [[w:John Morton (cardinal)|John Morton]], A.D. 1279–1500.|title=England’s Sacred Synods. A Constitutional History of the Convocations of the Clergy, from the Earliest Records of Christianity in Britain to the Date of the Promulgation of the Present Book of Common Prayer:{{nb...|Including a List of All Councils, Ecclesiastical as well as Civil, Held in England, in which the Clergy have been Concerned.}}|location=London|publisher=[[w:Rivington (publishers)|Rivingtons]],{{nb...|Waterloo Place.}}|year=1855|page=316|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=engZp79hlOkC&pg=PA316|oclc=7807822|passage=Sometimes also committees were appointed to hear the complaints of clergymen and form "'''gravamina'''" upon the evidence produced. And "'''gravamina'''" of such a formal and authoritative character, if emanating from the lower house, were usually presented by the prolocutor.}}
